        ; /S is bit 7 of the 81h mask, and all it does is put 10h where the AH=4Eh at
        ; 3EEAh will load CX from -- so "match directories as well" is spelled as an
        ; attribute rather than as a flag anyone tests.  The one place that does test it,
        ; 3F11h, is checking whether to skip "." and "..", which only matters when
        ; directories are being matched.
