        ; 5BF8h falls back to DEST_NAME_BUF built from the source.  The three bits then
        ; gate what follows: TRUENAME_DEST skips building DEST_TRUENAME for a device, so
        ; SAME_FILE_CHECK has no canonical pair to match on -- a device cannot be the file
        ; being read -- and 5E10h makes the AX=1817h call only for a real file.
        ;
        ; Bit 0 is tested three times, at 62F8h, 634Eh and 658Bh, so "is the destination a
        ; device" is asked at the truename, the read and the write.  And the reset is
        ; `and byte [COPY_DEST_FLAGS], 0F9h` at 5ACAh, clearing bits 1 and 2 and leaving
        ; bit 0 alone: COPY_NEXT_ARGUMENT
