        ; 6145  IS_CHAR_DEVICE        8B D8 B8 00 44 CD 21 F6 C2 80   handle in AX
        ; 6606  SRC_IS_DEVICE         B8 00 44 8B 1E E2 4D CD 21 ...  handle from memory
        ;
        ; The first pair is the frame split -- one copy in the resident half, one in the
        ; transient, because a near call cannot cross.  The third is not: SRC_IS_DEVICE
        ; is in the same frame as IS_CHAR_DEVICE and does the same test with the two
        ; instructions the other way round, because its handle comes from
        ; COPY_SRC_HANDLE rather than from AX.  Then each tests a different mode bit --
        ; COPY_DEST_BINARY here, COPY_SRC_BINARY there -- which is the actual reason for
        ; two.
