        ; FILEOP_DEST_POS has been established.  Every arm ends at one of three tails --
        ; AL=1 with a file in hand, AL=0 when there are none left, and AL=0FFh when
        ; something failed -- so the caller never has to know which arm ran.
        ;
        ; The third is not a flag but a number, and 628Ch closes both files before
        ; returning it, so a caller seeing 0FFh has nothing left to clean up.  6371h
        ; tells it from the other two with a *signed* compare, which is the only reason
        ; 0FFh works as a third answer in a register that already means two things.
