        ; Then COPY_BUF_SIZE_LO is the remainder, and that last write is the only one
        ; that can carry an end-of-file mark.  COPY_BUF_FULL is checked first: if the
        ; buffer still holds unwritten data there is more to come, so no mark is
        ; considered at all.
        ;
        ; What decides it is a ladder rather than a flag.  Bit 5 of COPY_FLAGS -- the
        ; destination's /B -- says no; bit 4, its /A, says yes; and only if neither was
        ; given does COPY_FLAGS_SAVED and then the source's own bits get a say.  An
        ; explicit switch on the destination wins, and the source's mode is what a copy
        ; inherits when nobody said.
