FCB_WILDCARD_NAME:
        ; VOL_SEARCH_FCB+8 — the image ships the FCB already built
        ; Not a constant anyone loads.  These eleven bytes are the name field of
        ; VOL_SEARCH_FCB, which begins eight bytes earlier, and the image holds the whole
        ; extended FCB already assembled:
        ;
        ; FF 00 00 00 00 00 08 00 3F 3F 3F 3F 3F 3F 3F 3F 3F 3F 3F
        ;
        ; That is 0FFh for an extended FCB, five reserved zeros, attribute 8 for a volume
        ; label, drive 0, and eleven wildcards.  SHOW_VOLUME_LABEL writes exactly those
        ; bytes again at 4CE8h before every search -- `mov al, 0FFh / stosb`, five zeros,
        ; `mov al, 8`, then `mov cx, 0Bh / mov al, "?" / rep stosb` -- so the copy in the
        ; image is never the one that gets used.
        ;
        ; Only +7 changes: 4D0Dh puts the drive there after the rebuild, which is the
        ; whole reason the rebuild exists.  The pre-built copy survives because the work
        ; area is loaded from the image and nothing zeroes this part of it.
        ;
        ; Nothing references 6E1Ch in either frame, which is what it looks like when a
        ; label names a field instead of an object.
        ; Format: FORMAT_STRING
        db      "???????????"                                  ;#6E1C: 3F 3F 3F 3F 3F 3F 3F 3F 3F 3F 3F

